{
  "id": "Compound::DB00595 - Gene::10864",
  "verbalization": "Oxytetracycline is linked to Slc22a7 through a series of molecular interactions that involve both direct and indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that Oxytetracycline, as a member of the tetracycline class, binds to Slc22a11, which is a transporter involved in the uptake of organic anions. This transporter, in turn, is involved in the transport of Slc22a7, indicating a potential role in the cellular uptake of certain compounds. The connection between Oxytetracycline and Slc22a7 is further supported by the direct binding of Minocycline, another tetracycline derivative, to Slc22a7, suggesting that the transport mechanism may be conserved across tetracycline analogs. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Oxytetracycline influences cellular processes through its interaction with transporters, potentially affecting the uptake of organic anions and their subsequent effects on cellular function.",
